# Copy to `.env` (git-ignored) and edit. Everything here is optional — with no
# `.env` at all, every script, hook, and build in this repo runs on defaults
# that are local and self-contained, and none of them point at anyone else's
# hosting account.
#
# Two loaders read this file automatically, so there is no flag to pass and no
# `export FOO=... ./script.sh` to remember:
#
#   scripts/env.sh              shell scripts and git hooks
#   website/scripts/load-env.js anything in website/ that runs on Node
#
# Both read this file first, then `website/.env`, so site-specific values
# override shared ones. Both leave an already-exported variable alone, so a CI
# secret or a one-off `FOO=bar npm run ...` always wins over the file.
#
# Site configuration (SITE_URL, ELEVENLABS_*) belongs in `website/.env` —
# see website/.env.example. It is read from here too, but keeping it next to
# the site it configures is the convention.

# --- Xcode / app signing -----------------------------------------------------
# The app's real signing seam is the git-ignored
# app/Config/Signing.local.xcconfig (see docs/ENVIRONMENT.md), which is what
# both Xcode and xcodebuild read. Setting the same names here as environment
# variables also works — xcodebuild takes build settings from the environment,
# and scripts/open-xcode.sh loads this file before launching Xcode so the GUI
# build sees them too. Prefer the xcconfig; use these only for a one-off build.
#
#   DEVELOPMENT_TEAM=ABCDE12345
#   BUNDLE_ID_PREFIX=com.yourname

# --- Git hook tuning ---------------------------------------------------------
# The post-commit / post-checkout hooks rebuild the Graphify knowledge graph.
# These are the knobs they already honor; they default to the values shown.
#
#   GRAPHIFY_FORCE=0             # 1 rebuilds even when nothing relevant changed
#   GRAPHIFY_MAX_WORKERS=1       # parallelism for the rebuild
#   GRAPHIFY_REBUILD_TIMEOUT=600 # seconds before the rebuild is abandoned
#   GRAPHIFY_OUT=graphify-out    # output directory
